Package: parkett
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: David M. Anderson <david.anderson@excelano.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://excelano.com/parkett/
Depends: libc6, libgcc-s1, libwayland-client0, libxkbcommon0, libxkbcommon-x11-0, libegl1, libvulkan1 | libgl1, libx11-6, libx11-xcb1, libxi6, libxcursor1, libxrandr2, desktop-file-utils, hicolor-icon-theme, shared-mime-info
Description: View Apache Parquet files
 Parkett opens an Apache Parquet file as a grid that scrolls through
 millions of rows, reading only the stretch in view, and beside it, on
 request, what the file says about itself: its schema, row groups, and each
 column's codec, encodings, sizes and statistics. Values are shown by their
 type, nested values as JSON. A selection copies as tab-separated rows, and
 the file or the columns selected export as CSV. It never writes Parquet.
 .
 The package declares the application/vnd.apache.parquet media type, which
 shared-mime-info does not, so a file manager knows a .parquet file and
 offers Parkett for it.
 .
 The executable links libc, libgcc and libm and nothing else the linker
 records; Zstandard is compiled in. The display stack, the graphics driver
 loader and the keyboard map libraries are opened by name at run time, so
 Depends is written by hand and packaging/linux/check-libraries.sh measures
 it against a running window on both display backends.
 .
 The last three packages own the dpkg triggers that rebuild the desktop,
 icon and media type caches, which is why this package carries no maintainer
 scripts.
